\caption(The same encoder has two optimizer states. Priors affect the discriminator, while reconstruction remains deterministic.)
\alttext(Images pass through E and G for reconstruction. Encoded data and explicit Gaussian prior samples enter D, whose real-label objective also trains E through a separate optimizer.)

> Hand losses at zero logits

At three zero pixel logits, any binary target row has reconstruction NLL3log2≈2.07944.
For target[1,0,1], the logit derivative is[−0.5,0.5,−0.5]. At zero discriminator logits,
L_D=2log2 and L_E,adv=log2. D wants real logits to increase and fake logits to decrease;
E's adversarial step wants fake logits to increase instead. Stable softplus avoids computing
log(sigmoid) after a probability has rounded to0 or1.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/aae_losses.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n           = dm::nn;
  const auto type       = n::DType::Float64;
  const auto logits     = n::zeros({1, 3}, type).requires_grad_(),
             target     = n::tensor({1., 0., 1.}, {1, 3}, type);
  const auto loss       = n::models::BernoulliPixelNll(logits, target);
  const auto derivative = n::grad(n::sum(loss), {logits})[0];
  if (std::abs(loss.item() - 3 * std::log(2.)) > 1e-14 ||
      n::max(n::abs(derivative - n::tensor({-.5, .5, -.5}, {1, 3}, type))).item() > 1e-14)
    return 1;
  auto real     = n::zeros({1, 1}, type).requires_grad_(),
       fake     = n::zeros({1, 1}, type).requires_grad_();
  const auto dl = n::mean(n::softplus(-real)) + n::mean(n::softplus(fake));
  const auto dg = n::grad(dl, {real, fake});
  const auto el = n::mean(n::softplus(-fake));
  const auto eg = n::grad(el, {fake})[0];
  if (std::abs(dl.item() - 2 * std::log(2.)) > 1e-14 || dg[0].item() != -.5 || dg[1].item() != .5 ||
      eg.item() != -.5)
    return 1;
  std::print(
      "Pixel NLL {:.9f}, pixel partials {}. D loss {:.9f}, E adversarial {:.9f}.\n",
      loss.item(),
      derivative.values_str(),
      dl.item(),
      el.item());
  std::vector<double> x, prior, fake_loss;
  for (int i = 0; i <= 80; ++i) {
    double v = -4 + i * .1;
    x.push_back(v);
    prior.push_back(std::log1p(std::exp(-v)));
    fake_loss.push_back(std::log1p(std::exp(v)));
  }
  auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.lines(x, prior, "real label / E adversarial", {37, 99, 235}, 2)
      .lines(x, fake_loss, "fake label / D encoded", {220, 38, 38}, 2)
      .x_label("discriminator logit")
      .y_label("single-example softplus loss")
      .title("D and E adversarial updates request opposite encoded labels")
      .save_svg("build/aae_losses.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Pixel NLL 2.079441542, pixel partials [[-0.5, 0.5, -0.5]]. D loss 1.386294361, E adversarial 0.693147181.
\image(figures/aae_losses.svg)
// result_end

\caption(The encoder adversarial curve coincides with the real-label loss; the two D terms are averaged separately.)
\alttext(Real-label softplus decreases with discriminator logit; fake-label softplus increases. At zero each term equals log2.)

For decoder probability R=σ(L), the reconstruction logit derivative is(R−X)/B: pixels are
summed, not averaged. D's prior derivative is(σ(s_r)−1)/P, its encoded derivative isσ(s_f)/B,
and E's adversarial encoded derivative is(σ(s_f)−1)/B. Tanh contributes1−h² at each hidden
layer. These signs and normalizations are preserved; changing to per-pixel mean would rescale
reconstruction gradients by784 and alter the source trajectory.

At an ideal population discriminator with compatible densities p(prior),q(encoded),
D*(z)=p(z)/(p(z)+q(z)) and the minimized discriminator loss is2log2−2JS(p||q).
That identity assumes an optimized discriminator with sufficient capacity. Here D is finite,
training is short, and deterministic codes of210 training observations form a finite empirical
support whereas a Gaussian is continuous. Exact equality of those two empirical/population
measures is impossible; a loss near2log2 from this small trained D cannot certify matching.
No per-example variational KL, exact marginal likelihood or ELBO is computed.

> Executed graph and independent parameter census

The graph collects the three scalar objectives for display; fitting uses their separate phases,
not the sum of this display vector. It includes the supplied prior branch and both uses of the
same discriminator. For tracing only, a788-value input packs one784-pixel image and one
four-value zero prior row, then splits them into explicitly labelled boundaries. The API and
fitting loop still take separate image and prior tensors.
The encoder owns12,628 scalars, decoder13,408 and discriminator97:26,133 across12 leaves.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/aae_architecture.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::ParameterStore e(3501), g(3511), d(3527);
  n::Module         model(
      [&](const n::Tensor& packed) {
        const auto x = n::slice_axis(packed, 1, 0, 784), prior = n::slice_axis(packed, 1, 784, 788);
        n::model_stage("Image probe /784 pixels", packed, x);
        n::model_stage("Supplied prior probe /4 values", packed, prior);
        auto o = n::models::AdversarialAutoencoder(e, g, d, x, prior);
        n::model_stage("Deterministic tanh/linear encoder", x, o.code);
        n::model_stage("Bernoulli decoder logits", o.code, o.logits);
        n::model_stage("D: supplied prior / real", prior, o.prior_logit);
        n::model_stage("D: encoded / fake", o.code, o.encoded_logit);
        n::model_stage(
            "Summed-pixel reconstruction NLL",
            std::vector<n::Tensor>{x, o.logits},
            o.reconstruction_loss);
        n::model_stage(
            "Discriminator real+fake loss",
            std::vector<n::Tensor>{o.prior_logit, o.encoded_logit},
            o.discriminator_loss);
        n::model_stage("Encoder non-saturating loss", o.encoded_logit, o.adversarial_loss);
        return n::stack({o.reconstruction_loss, o.discriminator_loss, o.adversarial_loss}, 0);
      },
      "AAE: three displayed objectives / independent update groups");
  n::ModelPlotOptions options;
  options.style                 = n::ModelPlotStyle::Graph;
  options.detail                = n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;
  options.max_neurons           = 8;
  options.sizing.spatial_scale  = n::ModelPlotScale::Linear;
  options.sizing.channel_scale  = n::ModelPlotScale::Linear;
  options.sizing.minimum_extent = 2;
  options.sizing.max_planes     = 6;
  const auto figure             = model.plot(n::zeros({1, 788}), options);
  if (e.count() != 12628 || g.count() != 13408 || d.count() != 97 ||
      figure.parameter_count() != 26133)
    return 1;
  figure.save_svg("build/aae_architecture.svg");
  std::print(
      "| group | tensors | scalars |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| E | {} | {} |\n| G | {} | {} |\n| D | {} "
      "| {} |\n",
      e.size(),
      e.count(),
      g.size(),
      g.count(),
      d.size(),
      d.count());
}
```
