> The original known-factor lattice, prepared natively

This dataset is a local procedural teaching fixture, not a downloaded image benchmark. It
exhausts2 shapes(circle/square),3 sizes,7 horizontal positions and7 vertical positions. Radius
is size+2 and centre=(3x+5,3y+5) in28×28 pixels, with inclusive boundaries. Source ID is
(((shape×3+size)×7+x)×7+y). Residue(x+2y+size+3shape) mod7 assigns test0, validation1 and
fitting2–6, producing210/42/42 unique binary images, with each factor balanced in every split.
Rows retain ascending source IDs. Split-specific combinations are held out; this is not a
random IID split. The original loader independently regenerates all230,496 pixels and checks
all source IDs, factors, uniqueness, split residues and marginal balance.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const std::filesystem::path cache = dm::datasets::data_home();
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("beta-vae-assets", cache.string());
  auto arrays = n::load_npz((cache / "beta_vae/factors.npz").string());
  for (auto& [name, value] : arrays)
    if (name.ends_with("_images"))
      value = n::cast(value, n::DType::Float32);
  n::save_npz("build/aae_data.npz", arrays);
  std::filesystem::copy_file(
      cache / "beta_vae/manifest.json",
      "build/aae_data_manifest.json",
      std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
  std::print("| split | observations | pixel geometry |\n|---|---:|---|\n");
  for (const auto& [name, value] : arrays)
    if (name.ends_with("_images"))
      std::print("| {} | {} | 28 ×28 ×1 |\n", name, value.size(0));
}
