> Verification and limits

The core owns native lattice generation, stable per-image Bernoulli NLL and independent E/G/D
forward components. Complete fitting, optimizer state, selection and checkpoint restoration
remain editable C++. The original checker accepts all294 native images and230,496 pixels.
Native tests cover every small-model parameter first derivative, input/prior first and second
derivatives, separate prior batch sizes, field ownership, invalid inputs before creation and
three-phase isolation. A reconstruction-barrier test confirms that recomputing G gradients
after changing E would use a different snapshot. All original26 archives, exact batch order,
noise banks and phase/checkpoint arrays are compared with the executed original baseline.

This is one fixed-seed, tiny compositional experiment with21 minibatches. Reconstruction and
adversarial objectives can compete; four independent Adam states and correct phase isolation
do not guarantee convergence or meaningful generation. The Gaussian samples are discriminator
training inputs and code-only generation inputs, not reconstruction noise. The weaker-than-mean
MSE, finite-support limitation, diffuse images and lack of downstream evaluation remain part
of the result.
